      "body": "**Requesting repo:** gsmlg-opt/gaoxy on branch `codex/m3-h1-resource-foundation`\n\n**Severity:** blocker for our existing public H1 cancellation compatibility gate. We are continuing other unblocked work and preserving the exact assertion.\n\nA direct HTTP/1 request can return `{:error, :einval}` from its original Promise after `HTTP.RequestCompletion.abort_and_await(original, 3000)` returns `:ok`. This occurs after the loopback peer receives the complete request headers, while it withholds every response byte. We expect `{:error, :aborted}` for this cancellation.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Start a passive loopback TCP listener. Accept the connection and receive through the complete `\\r\\n\\r\\n` request header terminator. Notify the caller, send no response, and wait for the socket to close.\n2. Call `HTTP.fetch(url, http_version: :http1, http1_reuse: false, tls_backend: :ssl, redirect: :manual, decode_body: false, request_mode: :proxy, timeout: 3000)` and retain `HTTP.Promise.completion(promise)`.\n3. After the peer's complete-header notification, call `RequestCompletion.await(original, 0)` (returns `{:error, :cleanup_pending}`), `RequestCompletion.abort_and_await(original, 3000)` (returns `:ok`), then `Promise.await(promise, 3000)`.\n4. Require `{:error, :aborted}` from the Promise, actual peer closure, joined peer DOWN, and repeated original completion `:ok`.\n\nThe unchanged executable reproduction is `apps/gaoxy_proxy/test/http_fetch_completion_test.exs:8` in the requesting repo. Its SHA256 is `29d88592b122693154e4e0d5197910c65a2a5b2de4bcfe201f651afc474c09e6`.\n\n### Actual evidence and limits\n\nOn the coordinated Hex `http_fetch`/`http_core`/`http_runtime` 0.21.4 cohort, our source-stable 58-file run executed 845 tests with one failure, seed 33011, `ERL_FLAGS=+S 2:2`, exit 2. The exact Promise assertion at line 21 observed `{:error, :einval}` instead of `{:error, :aborted}`. Cleanup had returned `:ok`; later peer/repeated assertions did not execute after that failed assertion.\n\nThis is intermittent: an unchanged whole-file run passed 5/5, and a bounded 32-case public-only probe passed 32/32. The probe retained all results and confirmed peer closure, peer DOWN and repeated original completion for every case. These results do not erase the original failure or demonstrate a repair. There is no deterministic failing syscall trace yet.\n\nLocal evidence root: `docs/acceptance/evidence/m3/managed-h2-fixed-endpoint/1791956542961215590/`. Failing receipt: `pre-floor-full58-1792000443558300185.json`; log SHA256 `624260543bec4ab490c3cd738805d3026b4d53e3ebcf93298f7302971fc23f91`. Bounded probe receipt: `public-pre-head-cancel-repeat-diagnostic2-1792003696569237413.json`.\n\n### Source-supported race\n\n`apps/http_core/lib/http/request_lifecycle.ex:373-375` sends the owner `:abort` while cancelling the tracked socket; lines 475-477 apply linger and close it. After successful buffered sending, `apps/http_fetch/lib/http/socket_client.ex:558-568` calls `activate_socket` before entering `owner_loop`, which consumes the pending abort. `activate_socket` at lines 1954-1962 calls `setopts(active: :once)` and returns its raw error. `fail` at lines 1567-1584 preserves non-timeout errors, and `await_owner` at lines 1664-1666 forwards them to the Task/Promise result.\n\nIf cleanup closes the socket during post-send activation, a transport error can win over the pending cancellation. A racing final-send error is also possible. This explains a possible path to the observed result; the exact failing operation remains untraced. Successful logical cleanup can coexist with an incorrect Promise cancellation classification.\n\nThe v0.21.8 SocketClient and RequestLifecycle remain byte-identical to the installed 0.21.4 files, so upgrading to that release does not change these paths. Searches found no matching issue; the previous parser-error and old `:httpc` abort issues describe different triggers.\n\nPlease preserve cancellation classification when cleanup closes this pending request's socket, while retaining independent transport/protocol failures and existing cleanup guarantees. Add upstream regression coverage of cancellation during post-send activation/final send and publish a compatible coordinated release. This request concerns the observed Promise error classification, using real wire synchronization and public APIs.\n",
